#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 18 files across `domain/filing` and `domain/invoices`, "
"totaling 4,860 manifest-counted lines, 213,297 bytes, and 46,179 measured"
" `o200k_base` tokens. I read every assigned file in bounded slices "
"through its end. This is static analysis of the checked-in snapshot: I "
"did not import or execute the application, modify `src/`, run tests, or "
"independently validate the legal rules described in comments and "
"registry-facing code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:14
msgid "Product capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:16
msgid ""
"The filing domain supplies the typed records and validation ports for "
"building Modelo drafts from registry-backed casilla and row-binding "
"schemas. A value records whether it is literal, computed, inherited, "
"defaulted, or empty; computed values carry a formula-input trace. Casilla"
" and binding records preserve legal and source references, while binding "
"rows can retain typed row-source identity. The draft also carries the "
"taxpayer, period, registry snapshot coordinates, schema marker, findings,"
" lifecycle stamps, and approval-basis fingerprints. These structures give"
" application workflows enough material to review a draft, compare it with"
" upstream state, and identify the sources behind its figures draft and "
"value records (`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/schema.py`) approval basis "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/schema.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:18
msgid ""
"`ModeloValidator` compares a draft with its casilla collection: it "
"reports schema-version mismatches, unknown casillas, missing required "
"values, numeric constraint violations, and formula-trace divergence. An "
"optional deadline checker adds an overdue finding. Applying the result "
"returns a copy with findings and a status derived from severity: errors "
"leave it in draft, warnings promote it to validated, and no findings "
"promote it to ready-to-file validation pass "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/validator.py`) status application "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/validator.py`). Protocols keep the "
"application layer dependent on narrow interfaces for schemas, deadlines, "
"profiles, and typed inputs instead of importing concrete sibling services"
" filing ports (`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/protocols.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:20
msgid ""
"For export headers, the domain represents a reviewed AEAT software "
"identity separately from Cadrumo’s explicit development mock. The record "
"requires four-byte program and nine-byte developer identifiers, unique "
"evidence references, and a non-empty evidence tuple. Its grade is derived"
" from the identifiers, so callers cannot relabel the all-zero mock as "
"reviewed. The helper loads the mock values from governed facts and marks "
"the evidence as not AEAT-certified; the package version is separately "
"rendered as the four-character `Aux/VERSION` token when its format fits "
"software identity validation "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/software_identity.py`) version projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/software_identity.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:22
msgid ""
"The invoice domain models issued and received documents as strict "
"immutable records with typed lines, counterparty and identification "
"facts, legal-mention evidence, payment status, transaction links, FX "
"provenance, and optional Modelo 347 and OSS/IOSS axes. It derives a "
"stable identifier from invoice direction, number, issue date, "
"counterparty tax ID, currency, and total. Line and invoice validators "
"enforce basic arithmetic, nonnegative monetary inputs, dated IVA-rate "
"availability, exact aggregate totals, FX-stamp completeness, retention "
"and surcharge bounds, invoice-class conditions, and registry-backed "
"OSS/IOSS pairing invoice identity "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`) invoice record "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`) arithmetic and totals "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:24
msgid ""
"`decompose_invoice` classifies whether those records have enough grounded"
" information for euro aggregation. It produces either complete non-"
"optional components (base, IVA, retention, recargo, suplido, total and "
"cash) or explicit defects such as undeclared IVA treatment, missing "
"taxable base, impossible category for invoice direction, category/cuota "
"contradiction, or unresolved FX. The classifier leaves the original "
"invoice in the catalogue and makes incomplete records visible for review "
"rather than refusing capture or treating unknown components as legal "
"zeroes decomposition outcome "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/decomposition.py`) classifier "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/decomposition.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:26
msgid ""
"Invoice service helpers create a new catalogue with a transaction ID "
"linked to an invoice, propose deterministic amount-and-name "
"reconciliation candidates, and report one-sided invoice/transaction "
"links. Suggestions require the expected cash-flow direction and amount "
"match; counterparty-name overlap raises the score but cannot qualify a "
"pair by itself. Persistence and coordinated updates across both "
"catalogues are application-layer responsibilities linking and suggestions"
" (`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/service.py`) consistency check "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/service.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:28
msgid "How it works"
msgstr "Cómo funciona"

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:30
msgid ""
"Filing records are frozen Pydantic models. Construction enforces the "
"`EMPTY`/`None` relationship and requires formula traces exactly for "
"computed values. A draft also checks that the profile and subject tax IDs"
" agree, its Modelo and filing period match the registry snapshot, its "
"schema marker names that revision, and no casilla or binding-row "
"coordinate is duplicated. The content-address function sorts values and "
"binding rows before hashing, and includes row-source identity only in the"
" controlled secure serialization context. The draft model deliberately "
"leaves final `draft_id` verification to the persistence save boundary, "
"which is outside this chunk draft invariants "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/schema.py`) stable content address "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/schema.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:32
msgid ""
"The invoice deserialization path normalizes dates, enum tokens, strings, "
"counterparty identity, currency, monetary values, collections, and "
"payment IDs before strict model validation. Nested lines coerce decimal "
"strings and resolve registry tokens; invoice-level validators then apply "
"the known operation or issue date to the IVA amount check. Foreign-"
"currency values convert only when a rate is stamped, otherwise euro "
"accessors return `None`; the rate, date, and source must be present "
"together and must be absent for EUR invoices normalization pipeline "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`) FX accessors and stamp rules "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`) line-rate check "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`). The catalogue rejects bare "
"unwrapped mappings and duplicate IDs, validates that mapping keys equal "
"invoice IDs, and freezes its invoice map catalogue shape "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:34
msgid "Knowledge and data"
msgstr "Conocimiento y datos"

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:36
msgid ""
"Filing requirements, casilla constraints, formula inputs, binding "
"sources, schema revisions, and product mock identity values are "
"externalized through registry-backed interfaces or references carried on "
"the draft. The validator consumes the schema provider’s current "
"collection; it does not itself compute tax totals or establish registry "
"authority. A schema-version mismatch is a warning, while unknown casillas"
" and formula divergence are errors. The optional deadline checker is an "
"explicit caller-supplied dependency, so a validator constructed without "
"one reports no deadline finding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:38
msgid ""
"Invoice enum fields and classification vocabularies are resolved through "
"the governed registry, and date-sensitive IVA rate arithmetic is "
"delegated to the IVA facade. The record also stores what appeared on the "
"document—addresses, legal notices, exemption references, FX source and "
"date—rather than claiming to regenerate that evidence from current "
"profile data. Counterparty identification is distinct from country of "
"establishment; where absent, downstream classification is expected to "
"hold the row for review rather than infer a tax-registration country "
"counterparty normalization "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/normalization.py`) identification gate "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`). No AI or network behavior is "
"present in these domain files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:40
msgid "Security and safety"
msgstr "Seguridad y protección"

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:42
msgid ""
"The filing data models use strict immutable configurations. Binding "
"records hide row-source identity from ordinary representations and "
"serialization, exposing it only when a serializer receives the literal "
"`secure_modelo_binding_value=True` context. That is a useful redaction "
"boundary for ordinary dumps, but it is a convention at the serialization "
"call site, not authorization: any caller able to supply that context can "
"include the identity. Likewise, a content digest and reference on "
"software-identity evidence establish shape, not independent proof that "
"the evidence authorizes the identifiers binding serializer "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/schema.py`) evidence record "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/filing/software_identity.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:44
msgid ""
"Invoice records contain tax IDs, addresses, names, amounts, payment "
"links, and source-file provenance. These models validate and normalize "
"those fields but do not implement encryption, access checks, external "
"transmission, or a general redaction funnel. Those controls must be "
"assessed in persistence and application callers. Link suggestions are "
"advisory, not automatic writes; `verify_link_consistency` provides an "
"explicit diagnostic for either side missing its reciprocal link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:46
msgid "Implementation assessment"
msgstr "Evaluación de la implementación"

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:48
msgid ""
"The strongest local controls are cross-field coherence and explicit "
"provenance: draft values cannot contradict their declared kind, duplicate"
" coordinates are refused, registry revision and period are linked, "
"invoice totals reconcile exactly to line totals, and incomplete FX "
"provenance cannot silently look like a conversion. Errors distinguish "
"invoice validation, catalogue, link, and missing-record cases. The filing"
" validator separates informational required-text gaps from blocking "
"operator omissions, and it makes deadline checking an explicit injected "
"capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:50
msgid ""
"Several temporal and identity boundaries warrant follow-up. First, "
"deserializing a line whose `iva_rate` is a string resolves that token "
"against `today_madrid()`, although the enclosing invoice checks whether "
"the rate was in force on `operation_date or issued_at`. The same current-"
"date resolution is used for `oss_rate_kind`. If registry token membership"
" changes across time, historical invoices may fail to rehydrate even "
"where the token was valid on the invoice date line input coercion "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`) dated invoice check "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`). Second, simplified-invoice "
"tax-ID applicability is queried using today’s date and is evaluated "
"during invoice-class validation, rather than receiving the invoice’s "
"issue or operation date. If the governed applicability changes, "
"historical records can be judged against current facts; confirm whether "
"the authority fact is intentionally timeless applicability query "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`) validation use "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:52
msgid ""
"Third, the invoice hash excludes the separate `series` and "
"`invoice_class` fields. Two documents with identical hashed fields but "
"different series can therefore map to one catalogue key; whether that can"
" happen in production depends on how callers populate `invoice_number` "
"relative to `series` hash fields "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`) separate series field "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`). Fourth, reconciliation "
"compares `transaction.raw.amount` with `grand_total - retention_amount` "
"in the invoice’s native currency and does not use `grand_total_eur`; if "
"raw transaction amounts are euro-normalized, foreign-currency invoices "
"can receive incorrect suggestions. The transaction amount convention and "
"any upstream conversion need cross-module confirmation reconciliation "
"amount (`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/service.py`) euro accessor "
"(`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:54
msgid ""
"The invoice line’s `spending_category_id` is explicitly documented as "
"written and persisted but not read by a production consumer in this "
"domain, so it should not be described as an active classification "
"capability line field (`src/cadrumo/domain/invoices/models.py`). No "
"assigned tests are present in this chunk. Static inspection cannot "
"confirm whether application constructors always supply a pinned registry "
"operation, whether draft IDs are checked at every durable write, whether "
"deadlines are always injected, or whether FX-normalized transaction "
"amounts match the reconciliation helper’s assumption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:56
msgid "Dependencies and follow-up"
msgstr "Dependencias y seguimiento"

#: ../../technical/articles/142-filing-drafts-and-invoice-records.md:58
msgid ""
"Synthesis should trace the filing builder and draft repository to verify "
"content-address checks, approval-basis recomputation, hidden row-source "
"handling, and deadline-checker wiring. It should trace invoice import and"
" repository rehydration for historical token resolution and pinned-"
"authority scope; inspect the invoice-number/series construction contract;"
" and compare transaction amount units with invoice reconciliation. The "
"persistence and export layers should establish encryption, permissions, "
"redaction, coordinated link writes, and whether the development "
"identity’s grade remains visible to operators."
msgstr ""

